    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b7b646e8-df49-5fd0-a2c8-2f19e7d42eb1",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - y + 2 z &=-6 \\\\ 2 x - y + 7 z &=-15 \\\\ x - y + 3 z &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 7 & -15 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 7 & -15 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1 \\\\ y &=3 \\\\ z &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=1$, $y=3$, and $z=-2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle 1,3,-2\\rangle$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
