      ":question/id": "e777bfae-0e20-5f30-8934-f7019a035464",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+4y-z &=11 \\\\ x+y &=2 \\\\ 2x+2y+z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 4 & -1 & 11 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 4 & -1 & 11 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & \u2194{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
